From: Mobile BEAM Build <build@mobile-beam.local>
Subject: [PATCH] xcomp: Fix iOS builds for OTP 28

Two fixes for iOS cross-compilation in OTP 28:

1. DED_LD/DED_LDFLAGS - OTP 28 added OSSF security hardening flags that
   add -fstack-protector-strong to DED_LDFLAGS. This flag works with the
   C compiler as linker driver but fails when DED_LD is the raw linker.
   Fix: Use $CC (C compiler) as DED_LD instead of $LD (raw linker), and
   set proper DED_LDFLAGS with -undefined suppress for cross-compilation.

2. runtime_tools native drivers - These require ERTS symbols that are not
   available during cross-compilation, and dynamic loading isn't supported
   on iOS anyway.
   Fix: Add SKIP file for runtime_tools/c_src only.

---
 lib/runtime_tools/c_src/SKIP             | 1 +
 xcomp/erl-xcomp-arm-ios.conf             | 4 ++--
 xcomp/erl-xcomp-arm64-ios.conf           | 4 ++--
 xcomp/erl-xcomp-arm64-iossimulator.conf  | 4 ++--
 xcomp/erl-xcomp-host-iossimulator.conf   | 4 ++--
 xcomp/erl-xcomp-x86_64-iossimulator.conf | 4 ++--
 6 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/runtime_tools/c_src/SKIP b/lib/runtime_tools/c_src/SKIP
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lib/runtime_tools/c_src/SKIP
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Dynamic drivers not supported on iOS (no dynamic loading)
diff --git a/xcomp/erl-xcomp-arm-ios.conf b/xcomp/erl-xcomp-arm-ios.conf
--- a/xcomp/erl-xcomp-arm-ios.conf
+++ b/xcomp/erl-xcomp-arm-ios.conf
@@ -120,10 +120,10 @@ LDFLAGS="-L$XCOMP_SDKROOT/usr/lib/ -lc++ -v"
 ## *NOTE*! Either set all or none of the `DED_LD*' variables.

 # * `DED_LD' - Linker for Dynamically loaded Erlang Drivers.
-DED_LD=$LD
+DED_LD="$CC"

 # * `DED_LDFLAGS' - Linker flags to use with `DED_LD'.
-DED_LDFLAGS="-L$XCOMP_SDKROOT/usr/lib/ -r -v"
+DED_LDFLAGS="-bundle -flat_namespace -undefined suppress"

 # * `DED_LD_FLAG_RUNTIME_LIBRARY_PATH' - This flag should set runtime library
 #   search path for shared libraries when linking with `DED_LD'.
